{
  "dom_id": "step-q64577",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14225445/assets/a9381ee6a4c0fb541f9459dd8c31fd994228c9cf6b42a2c4579f72cab96c37ae.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows a unit circle. Given that the $x$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $-0.7,$ which of the following is correct?",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14225445/assets/fab4d89dbe3697bb9e22b815939129bdb87f1919985edbf5c84628a1eb1d5853.png)\n\nAny point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe're given that $x=-0.7$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-0.7.\n$$",
